        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Roster countries: Yazaki — JPN, Sumitomo Electric — JPN, Aptiv — USA.\n\nOn roster country alone, Yazaki and Sumitomo Electric share the same country (Japan) and so would be treated alike; Aptiv (USA) differs.\n\nWhat the roster country does not tell you: it's a corporate/roster designation, not a country of origin for the goods. Wire harnesses are labour-intensive and typically assembled in third countries — Mexico, Morocco, the Philippines, Eastern Europe — regardless of where the parent company is domiciled. Import duty turns on the origin of the shipped goods (substantial transformation, tariff classification, and any trade-agreement qualification like USMCA), none of which is in this data. So this roster can't actually settle the duty question for any of the three; you'd need plant location and origin documentation per part.",
